From: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: queue inbound SOE requests in arrival order

An SA may have four requests in flight. A burst of inbound ESP fills
that window at once, and the rest of the burst went to software XFRM.
Software then delivered those packets ahead of the earlier ones still
in the engine, which reorders the inner flows, and decrypted them with
the much slower software AES-GCM.

Keep up to 32 prepared inbound requests per SA on a pending list and
hand them to the engine in arrival order whenever a slot frees: on a
completion, an error completion or an expiry, and from a work item when
an outbound PPE bind ends or the engine restarts after an expired SA.
The refill therefore runs in the completion NAPI context and not in the
deferral worker. Only a packet that finds the pending list full falls
back to software XFRM. The pending requests of an SA that dies are
dropped.

Signed-off-by: hurrhnn <hurrhnn@icmp.kr>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_soe.c
